table_name|column_order|column_name|data_type|description
bw_supplier|1|supplier_id|VARCHAR|Supplier key, e.g. SUP-014
bw_supplier|2|supplier_name|VARCHAR|Fictional supplier name
bw_supplier|3|cw_types_offered|VARCHAR|CW types the supplier provides, semicolon separated: Contractor, Consultant, BPO
bw_supplier|4|hq_country_code|VARCHAR|Country of the supplier's head office
bw_supplier|5|onboarded_date|DATE|First day the supplier could take service orders
bw_supplier|6|is_active|BOOLEAN|False once Arcadia stopped using the supplier
bw_rate_card|1|rate_card_id|VARCHAR|Rate card line key
bw_rate_card|2|fiscal_year|INTEGER|Arcadia fiscal year the line applies to (July to June)
bw_rate_card|3|country_code|VARCHAR|Country where the work is done
bw_rate_card|4|cw_type|VARCHAR|Contractor, Consultant or BPO
bw_rate_card|5|role_family|VARCHAR|Development, QA, Data, Analyst, Project Delivery, Architecture, Design, Operations; BPO: Security, Facilities, Service Desk, Customer Support
bw_rate_card|6|seniority|VARCHAR|Junior, Mid, Senior or Lead
bw_rate_card|7|rate_type|VARCHAR|Hourly, or Monthly for BPO
bw_rate_card|8|billing_currency|VARCHAR|USD: the card is kept in USD; an order billing in local currency converts the target at the approval date's ECB rate
bw_rate_card|9|rate_low|DECIMAL|Bottom of the band
bw_rate_card|10|rate_target|DECIMAL|Target rate
bw_rate_card|11|rate_high|DECIMAL|Top of the band
bw_contingent_worker|1|bw_worker_id|VARCHAR|Bridgeway worker key, e.g. BW00012345. Bridgeway never stores the Keystone person ID
bw_contingent_worker|2|first_name|VARCHAR|Fictional
bw_contingent_worker|3|last_name|VARCHAR|Fictional
bw_contingent_worker|4|email|VARCHAR|Work email issued for the engagement (fictional domain)
bw_contingent_worker|5|supplier_id|VARCHAR|-> bw_supplier
bw_contingent_worker|6|cw_type|VARCHAR|Contractor, Consultant or BPO
bw_contingent_worker|7|original_start_date|DATE|First day of the first engagement under this Bridgeway ID
bw_contingent_worker|8|created_date|DATE|Day the supplier submitted the worker
bw_service_order|1|service_order_id|VARCHAR|Service order key, e.g. SO0012345
bw_service_order|2|bw_worker_id|VARCHAR|-> bw_contingent_worker
bw_service_order|3|supplier_id|VARCHAR|-> bw_supplier
bw_service_order|4|order_type|VARCHAR|New engagement, or Renewal of an earlier order for the same worker
bw_service_order|5|renews_service_order_id|VARCHAR|The order this one renews; empty for a new engagement
bw_service_order|6|opened_date|DATE|Manager raised the request
bw_service_order|7|submitted_date|DATE|Supplier submitted the worker
bw_service_order|8|approved_date|DATE|Order approved; empty if never approved
bw_service_order|9|final_status|VARCHAR|Status of the current revision at the extract date
bw_service_order_revision|1|revision_id|VARCHAR|Revision key
bw_service_order_revision|2|service_order_id|VARCHAR|-> bw_service_order
bw_service_order_revision|3|revision_no|INTEGER|0 for the original order, then 1, 2, ...
bw_service_order_revision|4|revision_reason|VARCHAR|Original or Renewal (revision 0), Extension, Rate change, Early end, Cost center change, Manager change, Office change, Closure
bw_service_order_revision|5|effective_start_date|DATE|First day the revision is in effect
bw_service_order_revision|6|effective_end_date|DATE|Last day in effect (inclusive); empty for the current revision
bw_service_order_revision|7|is_current|BOOLEAN|True on exactly one revision per order
bw_service_order_revision|8|status|VARCHAR|Pending Approval, Approved, Closed, Withdrawn, Rejected. Whether the worker is working on a date comes from the assignment dates, not the status
bw_service_order_revision|9|assignment_start_date|DATE|First working day of the assignment
bw_service_order_revision|10|assignment_end_date|DATE|Last working day of the assignment as this revision states it
bw_service_order_revision|11|closed_date|DATE|Day the order was closed in Bridgeway; empty while open
bw_service_order_revision|12|role_family|VARCHAR|See bw_rate_card
bw_service_order_revision|13|seniority|VARCHAR|Junior, Mid, Senior or Lead
bw_service_order_revision|14|job_title|VARCHAR|Title on the order
bw_service_order_revision|15|cost_center_code|VARCHAR|Cost center as typed on the order (text, not validated against Keystone)
bw_service_order_revision|16|hiring_manager_email|VARCHAR|Arcadia manager who owns the order
bw_service_order_revision|17|office_code|VARCHAR|Arcadia office where the work is done
bw_service_order_revision|18|bill_rate|DECIMAL|Rate in billing currency: per hour, or per month for BPO. Applies from the revision's effective date
bw_service_order_revision|19|rate_type|VARCHAR|Hourly or Monthly
bw_service_order_revision|20|billing_currency|VARCHAR|ISO currency code
bw_service_order_revision|21|hours_per_week|DECIMAL|Contracted hours; empty for monthly BPO orders
bw_timesheet_month|1|timesheet_id|VARCHAR|Timesheet key: one per worker x service order x month x rate (a month whose rate changed has two)
bw_timesheet_month|2|bw_worker_id|VARCHAR|-> bw_contingent_worker
bw_timesheet_month|3|service_order_id|VARCHAR|-> bw_service_order
bw_timesheet_month|4|month_end_date|DATE|Month billed
bw_timesheet_month|5|billed_hours|DECIMAL|Approved hours; 0 for monthly BPO orders
bw_timesheet_month|6|billed_units|DECIMAL|Hours for hourly orders; months (1.0, or a fraction in start and end months) for BPO
bw_timesheet_month|7|bill_rate|DECIMAL|Rate applied
bw_timesheet_month|8|billing_currency|VARCHAR|ISO currency code
bw_timesheet_month|9|billed_amount_local|DECIMAL|billed_units x bill_rate
ks_contingent_worker|1|ks_record_id|VARCHAR|Record key
ks_contingent_worker|2|person_id|VARCHAR|Keystone person ID, the same W... key space as employees
ks_contingent_worker|3|bw_worker_id|VARCHAR|Bridgeway worker ID as Keystone stored it from the feed; can be blank or mistyped
ks_contingent_worker|4|effective_start_date|DATE|First day the version applies
ks_contingent_worker|5|effective_end_date|DATE|Last day (inclusive); empty for the current version
ks_contingent_worker|6|change_source|VARCHAR|Feed, HR Ops or Manager: who wrote the version
ks_contingent_worker|7|feed_event_id|VARCHAR|-> feed_bridgeway_keystone_event when change_source = Feed
ks_contingent_worker|8|first_name|VARCHAR|As Keystone holds it
ks_contingent_worker|9|last_name|VARCHAR|As Keystone holds it
ks_contingent_worker|10|cw_type|VARCHAR|Contractor, Consultant or BPO
ks_contingent_worker|11|supplier_name|VARCHAR|Free text as fed; Keystone has no supplier table
ks_contingent_worker|12|status|VARCHAR|Active or Inactive
ks_contingent_worker|13|contract_start_date|DATE|As Keystone knows it
ks_contingent_worker|14|contract_end_date|DATE|As Keystone knows it; Keystone inactivates the worker the day after
ks_contingent_worker|15|inactive_reason|VARCHAR|Contract ended, Ended early, Converted to employee, Manual; empty while active
ks_contingent_worker|16|department_id|VARCHAR|-> dim_department
ks_contingent_worker|17|cost_center_id|VARCHAR|-> dim_cost_center
ks_contingent_worker|18|location_id|VARCHAR|-> dim_location
ks_contingent_worker|19|manager_worker_id|VARCHAR|Arcadia employee the worker reports to (-> dim_worker)
feed_bridgeway_keystone_event|1|feed_event_id|VARCHAR|Event key
feed_bridgeway_keystone_event|2|revision_id|VARCHAR|-> bw_service_order_revision that caused the event
feed_bridgeway_keystone_event|3|bw_worker_id|VARCHAR|-> bw_contingent_worker
feed_bridgeway_keystone_event|4|event_type|VARCHAR|New Worker, Extension, Early End, Rate Change, Attribute Change, Renewal, Closure
feed_bridgeway_keystone_event|5|sent_date|DATE|Day Bridgeway sent the change
feed_bridgeway_keystone_event|6|applied_date|DATE|Day Keystone applied it; empty if it failed
feed_bridgeway_keystone_event|7|outcome|VARCHAR|Applied, Applied Late, Partly Applied, Failed
feed_bridgeway_keystone_event|8|error_text|VARCHAR|Integration message for failures and partial loads
ref_source_system|1|system_code|VARCHAR|KS, BW, INT, WH or PUB
ref_source_system|2|system_name|VARCHAR|System name
ref_source_system|3|system_type|VARCHAR|What kind of system it is
ref_source_system|4|record_of|VARCHAR|What it is the system of record for
ref_source_system|5|used_by|VARCHAR|Who works in it
ref_source_system|6|extract|VARCHAR|How the warehouse receives it
ref_raw_table_lineage|1|table_name|VARCHAR|Raw table
ref_raw_table_lineage|2|system_code|VARCHAR|-> ref_source_system
ref_raw_table_lineage|3|module|VARCHAR|Module of the source system
ref_raw_table_lineage|4|grain|VARCHAR|One row per ...
ref_raw_table_lineage|5|history_type|VARCHAR|Type 1, SCD Type 2, Dated, Transaction, Accumulating snapshot, Versioned, Effective-dated
ref_raw_table_lineage|6|added_in_release|INTEGER|Warehouse release that added the table
ref_raw_column|1|table_name|VARCHAR|Raw table
ref_raw_column|2|column_order|INTEGER|1-based position in the extract
ref_raw_column|3|column_name|VARCHAR|Column
ref_raw_column|4|data_type|VARCHAR|Type staging casts to
ref_raw_column|5|description|VARCHAR|What it holds
